# Mainstream browse

Organise a large help collection into topics people already recognise, and keep it no deeper than it needs to be. People scan familiar subjects faster than clever categories. For example, “Lighting” and “Heating” work as topics. A household with a handful of guides needs one flat list and no hierarchy.

## When to use it

Use it for a large household help collection or documentation catalogue. Start with subjects people recognise, such as lighting, heating or maintaining the system. Keep broad subjects distinct from detailed task links.

## Structure and behaviour

Give a short introduction and plainly labelled topic links. Add a second level only where it reduces scanning. Alphabetical order suits a known-item list and task priority suits a curated one. Say which you chose and keep it stable. The [level one](mainstream-browse/level-one.html) and [level two](mainstream-browse/level-two.html) pages cover each level.

## Home Assistant boundary

Do not import a government taxonomy or popularity lists. The theme does not change Home Assistant areas, floors or labels. Navigation uses configured routes and does not suggest an entity has only one organisational relationship.

